# Irreplaceable assets - the ones whose loss stops the product.
#
# Format:  name | date RESTORING was last verified | period, days
#
# The date is not when the copy was made. It is when something was restored
# FROM that copy and the restored thing was seen to work. A copy you have never
# restored from is not a copy.
#
# There are no paths here on purpose: a file listing where your secrets live is
# a map in its own right. The name is enough for you to know what is meant.
#
# never - if restoring has not been verified even once.

# App signing key          | never | 90
# Licence signing key      | never | 90
# Store publishing account | never | 180
